      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Oakville Historical Society, founded in 1953, preserves the town’s archives and offers exhibits in the historic Thomas House.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.oakvillehistory.org/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Oakville was officially declared a distinct appellation within the Napa Valley AVA in 1993, now hosting 24 wineries and over 5,000 acres of vineyards.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oakville%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The name Oakville comes from the dense groves of dark green valley oaks that once covered the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oakville%2C_California",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
